{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208513-combat-question","id":1208513,"title":"Combat question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-18T12:05:39-07:00","id":1208513,"title":"Combat question","content":"So tell me if this works? One PC is attacked at close range by three NPC's. In the first round, the PC crashes NPC 1 gaining base 5 int + 5 crash bonus. Round two PC is now at 15 because the NPCs can't seem to land a hit, now the PC changes the target to NPC 2 and crash them for another 10 int which includes the bonus. now on the third round, the PC has 25 int which can be used in a decisive attack on NPC 3. So this leaves NPC 1 crashed NPC 2 crashed and NPC 3 with a 25 point decisive attack coming at them. So my question I guess is can you crash an NPC take the initiative and use it on someone else who is an NPC?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T12:13:26-07:00","id":1208518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1208513-combat-question#post1208513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So tell me if this works? One PC is attacked at close range by three NPC's. In the first round, the PC crashes NPC 1 gaining base 5 int + 5 crash bonus. Round two PC is now at 15 because the NPCs can't seem to land a hit, now the PC changes the target to NPC 2 and crash them for another 10 int which includes the bonus. now on the third round, the PC has 25 int which can be used in a decisive attack on NPC 3. So this leaves NPC 1 crashed NPC 2 crashed and NPC 3 with a 25 point decisive attack coming at them. So my question I guess is can you crash an NPC take the initiative and use it on someone else who is an NPC?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. NPC 3 is outta luck.Now, PC will be at 3 iniative next turn if they hit, leaving them open to Iniative Shift by the other 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T12:21:16-07:00","id":1208521,"title":"","content":"Yeah. It may seem a bit odd (last game, I did a bunch of withering attacks to an elite named mortal, then threw a 54-dice damage roll on a Dawn Caste), but a)it'd be way too awkward to track otherwise, b)it doesn't actually happen that often, in my experience, and c)sometimes it does seem pretty appropriate, especially with stunts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T12:31:29-07:00","id":1208526,"title":"","content":"It works like that, and is intended, and it's no surprise that a guy that overwhelms three enemies at once will kill either at any moment.<br /> <br /> And if the poor mofos 1 &amp; 2 land a withering hit after that, he's in trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T12:35:48-07:00","id":1208527,"title":"","content":"Also in general if you're using opponents of greatly mismatched scale, it can be reasonably assumed that since the idea of initiative is a momentum of combat, you're using the weaker fighter's lesser skill to interfere with the better fighter. Feints, misdirected attacks, and manuevering, to keep the better fighter off balance, and then just when it looks like you're about to take the lesser guy out, suddenly the better fighter has a HUGE problem he has to deal with because he doesn't see it coming now that you've changed tacks and gone for him all of a sudden.<br /> <br /> Usually ignoring either of your opponents in a fight is a huge mistake, but being good enough to use one fighter against the other? Sounds like a delightful combat style for a master warrior to me...<br /> <br /> (also, if it's super clear that the weaker fighter is trivial to the fight, the ST should just declare him such and move on... If he can meaningfully contribute, though, that's a different story)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T09:26:59-07:00","id":1208912,"title":"","content":"In addition to what everyone else said, the best defense is a good offense. If you can't keep someone from building initiative, you can land some hits and take it back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T10:01:14-07:00","id":1208931,"title":"","content":"Yeah &quot;Don't let players use one NPC as an initiative fountain if you can help it&quot; is a pretty solid rule.<br /> <br /> 3 evenly matched guys though? That's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}